 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "ketubot.28b.8",
   "daf": "28b",
   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "וְאֵין נֶאֱמָן לוֹמַר ״דֶּרֶךְ הָיָה לִפְלוֹנִי בַּמָּקוֹם הַזֶּה״, ״מַעֲמָד וּמִסְפֵּד הָיָה לִפְלוֹנִי בַּמָּקוֹם הַזֶּה״. מַאי טַעְמָא — אַפּוֹקֵי מָמוֹנָא לָא מַפְּקִינַן.",
   "en": "«And» the mishna states that «one is neither deemed credible to say: So-and-so had a path in this place;» nor to say: «So-and-so had» a tract of land where they would perform the ritual of «standing» and sitting «and» deliver «a eulogy in that place.» The Gemara asks: «What is the reason» that he is not deemed credible? It is due to the fact that «we do not remove money» from the possession of its presumptive owner on the basis of testimony about a matter that he witnessed as a minor."
  }
